  "slug": "machine-learning-assisted-83b8",
  "summary": "Recent preprints and a published package deliver installable design-plus-evaluation software for nucleic acid reagents.",
  "synthesis": "The dominant thread is computational design of nucleic acid reagents delivered as installable software. BaitBench, a Rust tool with CLI and GUI access, unifies hybrid capture probe design, assessment and thermodynamic simulation, and reports a correlation of rho=0.916 in its evaluation. PoolParty, a Python package, represents oligo pool DNA libraries as computational graphs, offering more than 50 mutagenesis, motif and barcode operations alongside design cards. What is new in this set is the pairing of design with in silico evaluation within a single tool, as in BaitBench. FastaGuard, DoAggregate, NBDC Data Tools and gcat/its_a_scam address sequence quality control, rare-variant aggregation, dataset construction and single-cell processing. They are adjacent infrastructure rather than part of the probe and library design thread.",
  "synthesis_model": "claude-haiku-5-5",
  "synthesized_on": "2026-11-05"
}
